From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Use the iPhOmarchy D21 touch driver

Replace apple-16k's apple_z2.c with the field-proven D21 driver from the
iPhOmarchy a11-port: chestnut touch-HV supply first in the power sequence,
SMC rBK3 rail control (ON 0x05020001), kext-faithful interrupt handling,
boot-sequence pokes with the 50 ms settle, 0x44 contact frames in signed
surface units with pressure validity and palm suppression, and bounded
runtime recovery that leaves an idle D21 alone. It carries the D21/D211
variant, is_d21() and the of_match entries, so no separate D21 driver
patch is needed.

Scoped to the t8015 series so other platforms keep their apple_z2.c.

Assisted-by: LLM
